WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.220
I'm Russ Michaels with Tercet Law.

2
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.520
If you have kids, one question matters more than any other.

3
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.240
If something happened to you and to their other parent, who would raise

4
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:16.420
them?

5
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.960
If you don't answer it, a judge will.

6
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:24.700
A will lets you name that person, someone who would raise your children

7
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.820
the way you would, and a backup in case they can't.

8
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.780
Texas courts give your choice priority.

9
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.520
Then there's the money.

10
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.620
Children can't manage an inheritance on their own.

11
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.060
Without a plan, it can end up under court supervision, and then go to them

12
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.980
at 18, all at once.

13
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.260
Now a trust lets you decide how it's used.

14
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.920
School, a first home, a safety net, on a timeline that makes sense.

15
00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.160
And if your family's blended, a clear plan matters even more.

16
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.540
It protects everyone you love, and it helps keep the peace.

17
00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.400
None of this is about expecting the worst.

18
00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.720
It's about knowing your kids will be okay no matter what.

19
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.720
There's a door here for you, so click the link below, and let's put a plan

20
00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.480
in place for the people who matter most.

